      "eli5": {
        "text": "A new version of the CLI tool was published today, which means anyone installing or updating it gets all the recent changes rolled up together. Most notably, the tool now supports a new Gravity Index feature for searching and browsing services directly from the command line. It also includes scam-risk scoring that uses an external fraud-detection service, and new authentication options that let connected third-party tools be managed without leaving the CLI. If you just use the CLI daily, the main thing you'd notice is the ability to run the new gravity-index command and the updated model pricing that reflects the latest token costs. Behind the scenes, this update also fixes a bug where pressing Enter on the keypad didn't work in the model selector menu on some Linux terminals.",
