      "eli5": {
        "text": "The free coding assistant can now be told not to automatically bring in a helper that reviews your code. This only matters if you're using the free tier of the tool and you call it with the noReview option turned on; otherwise nothing you see today changes. A couple of behind-the-scenes bits also landed at the same time: tool definitions sent to OpenAI-compatible providers now get their references resolved ahead of time so they won't fail upstream, and an optional tracking id was added that does nothing yet since nothing reads it.",
